{% doc %}
won-trust — render Won Toasts popularity signals on the PDP (Phase 8 bridge):
  • a visible "Bestseller" badge   ← product.metafields.won.bestseller
  • the factual units-sold count as Product.additionalProperty
                                    ← product.metafields.won.units_sold_30d

The metafields are written by the Won Toasts app (Pro). Keyed by the canonical
product URL so the count merges onto the product (same pattern as
[[won-schema-engine]]). Shows / emits NOTHING when the metafields are absent
(app not installed, Free plan, or product never sold) — never a fake claim. The
badge label is a merchant setting (localisable), so no runtime locale key.

@param {boolean} enabled - the section's show_bestseller toggle
@param {object} product - the product object
@param {string} label - the badge text (e.g. "Bestseller")
@example
{% render 'won-trust', enabled: section.settings.show_bestseller, product: product, label: section.settings.bestseller_label %}
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  assign units = product.metafields.won.units_sold_30d.value | default: 0
  assign is_best = product.metafields.won.bestseller.value | default: false
  assign badge = label | default: 'Bestseller'
-%}
{%- if enabled and product != blank -%}
  {%- if is_best -%}
    <span class="won-trust-badge">{{ badge }}</span>
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if units > 0 -%}
    {%- assign won_trust_url = product.url | prepend: shop.url -%}
    {%- capture won_trust_json -%}{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Product","@id":{{ won_trust_url | json }},"url":{{ won_trust_url | json }},"name":{{ product.title | json }},"additionalProperty":[{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"Units sold (30 days)","value":{{ units | json }}}]}{%- endcapture -%}
    <script type="application/ld+json">{{ won_trust_json | replace: '</', '<\/' }}</script>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  .won-trust-badge {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.4em;
    padding: 0.25em 0.7em; border-radius: var(--won-radius-pill, 999px);
    background: var(--won-accent); color: var(--won-accent-contrast, #fff);
    font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.02em; line-height: 1.4;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
